---
/**
 * /why section 01: how Abject differs. The thesis, the inversion as a split
 * (the old way ghosted), four comparisons that each use a different device
 * (A split, B paper field, C one large drawing, D split reversed), and the
 * closing thesis. Shared styles live in pages/why.astro (.why-page).
 */
import SectionHead from './ui/SectionHead.astro';

interface Props {
  num?: string;
}

const { num = '01' } = Astro.props;

const compared = [
  { id: 'vs-agent-frameworks', letter: 'A', name: 'Agent Frameworks', systems: 'OpenClaw · LangChain · CrewAI' },
  { id: 'vs-tool-protocols', letter: 'B', name: 'Tool Protocols', systems: 'MCP · Claude Skills · Function Calling' },
  { id: 'vs-orchestration', letter: 'C', name: 'Orchestration', systems: 'AutoGen · Subagents · ReAct' },
  { id: 'vs-visual-interface', letter: 'D', name: 'Visual Interface', systems: 'ChatGPT · Claude · Terminal Agents' },
];
---

<section id="symbiogenesis" class="why-sec symbio-section">
  <div class="container">

    <SectionHead num={num} kicker="Symbiogenesis" title="How is Abject different?">
      An AI agent in Abject is just another abject. So is every tool.
    </SectionHead>

    <div class="poster">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="standfirst">
          A chatbot gives you answers that scroll away. An app store gives you apps that are the
          same for everyone and can't talk to each other. Abject is short for AI Object. An abject
          is a little computer with its own window and its own memory, and it can explain its own
          source code when you ask. It keeps working after you close the chat. It talks to the
          other abjects, and some of them it made.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI agents are the wrong abstraction. They don't scale. Agent frameworks are
          hierarchies. MCP is a band-aid. A2A is a band-aid. Everyone is building plumbing between
          things that shouldn't need plumbing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Abject has nothing to plumb. Everything in the system is an abject, from the agents and
          the tools to the registry that finds them. The whole system is built as a bunch of
          objects communicating with each other, Smalltalk or Erlang style, where each object has
          an <em>ask</em> handler. That's how the internet works too. Since the first message
          went over ARPANET in 1969, all the atoms of the internet have been replaced and it has
          never shut down. Objects talking to objects is what works. We have proof. It runs the
          world.
        </p>
      </div>
      <nav class="poster-side rindex" aria-label="Compared here">
        <p class="rindex-label">Compared here</p>
        <ol>
          {compared.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${c.id}`}>
                <span class="ri-n">{c.letter}</span>
                <span class="ri-t">{c.name}</span>
                <span class="ri-s">{c.systems}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <!-- The inversion: the old way ghosted against the mesh -->
    <div class="split inv-split">
      <figure class="ghost">
        <p class="side-label"><s>The Old Way</s></p>
        <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 440px" viewBox="0 0 380 100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="The old way: an Agent issues one-way commands to a passive Tool">
          <defs>
            <marker id="sy-old-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <rect class="n-old shadow" x="6" y="22" width="100" height="46"/>
          <text class="lbl t-old-hi" x="56" y="50" text-anchor="middle">Agent</text>
          <line class="ln-old" x1="108" y1="45" x2="164" y2="45" marker-end="url(#sy-old-mk)"/>
          <text class="note" x="136" y="35" text-anchor="middle">commands</text>
          <rect class="n-old" x="168" y="22" width="100" height="46"/>
          <text class="lbl t-old" x="218" y="50" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="284" y="40">Agent decides.</text>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="284" y="57">Tool obeys.</text>
          <text class="note note-i" x="284" y="82">always one-way.</text>
        </svg>
      </figure>
      <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <figure>
        <p class="side-label hand">The Abject way</p>
        <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 480px" viewBox="0 0 380 196" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="The inversion: equal abjects talk in both directions, and any abject can create a new abject that joins as an equal">
          <defs>
            <marker id="sy-inv-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>

          <!-- Three equals, talking both ways -->
          <rect class="n shadow" x="6" y="14" width="100" height="44"/>
          <text class="lbl" x="56" y="41" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>
          <rect class="n shadow" x="140" y="14" width="100" height="44"/>
          <text class="lbl" x="190" y="41" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>
          <rect class="n shadow" x="274" y="14" width="100" height="44"/>
          <text class="lbl" x="324" y="41" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>

          <line class="ln-live" x1="109" y1="36" x2="137" y2="36" marker-start="url(#sy-inv-mk)" marker-end="url(#sy-inv-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-live" x1="243" y1="36" x2="271" y2="36" marker-start="url(#sy-inv-mk)" marker-end="url(#sy-inv-mk)"/>

          <!-- Any abject can create a new one -->
          <line class="ln-live" x1="190" y1="60" x2="190" y2="118" marker-end="url(#sy-inv-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live note-i" x="182" y="94" text-anchor="end">creates</text>

          <rect class="n-key shadow" x="140" y="122" width="100" height="44"/>
          <text class="lbl t-key" x="190" y="149" text-anchor="middle">Abject*</text>

          <!-- ...and the new one joins the conversation as an equal -->
          <line class="ln-live-dash" x1="243" y1="136" x2="312" y2="64" marker-start="url(#sy-inv-mk)" marker-end="url(#sy-inv-mk)"/>
          <text class="note note-live note-i" x="276" y="128">joins as</text>
          <text class="note note-live note-i" x="276" y="142">an equal</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="dg-cap"><span class="cap-line">No hierarchy. Any abject can create a new one, and it joins as an equal.</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <!-- A: a split, the old way ghosted -->
    <article class="cmp" id="vs-agent-frameworks">
      <header class="cmp-head">
          <span class="cmp-letter" aria-hidden="true">A</span>
          <h3 class="cmp-title">Agent Frameworks</h3>
          <span class="cmp-systems">OpenClaw &middot; LangChain &middot; CrewAI</span>
        </header>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="ghost">
          <p class="side-label">Them <span class="sub">hub and spoke</span></p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 408px" viewBox="0 0 340 150" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Hub and spoke: one Agent sends one-way calls to three silent Tools">
            <defs>
              <marker id="sa-l-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <rect class="n-old shadow" x="120" y="10" width="100" height="36"/>
            <text class="lbl t-old-hi" x="170" y="33" text-anchor="middle">Agent</text>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="142" y1="46" x2="74" y2="80" marker-end="url(#sa-l-mk)"/>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="170" y1="46" x2="170" y2="80" marker-end="url(#sa-l-mk)"/>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="198" y1="46" x2="266" y2="80" marker-end="url(#sa-l-mk)"/>
            <rect class="n-old" x="25" y="84" width="90" height="32"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="70" y="104" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text>
            <rect class="n-old" x="125" y="84" width="90" height="32"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="170" y="104" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text>
            <rect class="n-old" x="225" y="84" width="90" height="32"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="270" y="104" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text>
            <text class="note note-i" x="170" y="140" text-anchor="middle">silent, passive, one-way</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">In OpenClaw, skills are add-ons the agent calls. LangChain chains tools into workflows. CrewAI hands tools to roles. In all of them the tools are passive. They run when called and then go quiet. OpenClaw's ACP lets agents talk to agents, but the skills still can't say anything.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <p class="side-label hand">Abject <span class="sub">objects that talk</span></p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 456px" viewBox="0 0 380 156" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Objects that talk: three abjects, one of them an agent, each able to ask any other how it works; there is no top">
            <defs>
              <marker id="sa-r-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <line class="ln-live" x1="150" y1="42" x2="92" y2="84" marker-start="url(#sa-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sa-r-mk)"/>
            <line class="ln-live" x1="230" y1="42" x2="288" y2="84" marker-start="url(#sa-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sa-r-mk)"/>
            <line class="ln-live" x1="146" y1="99" x2="234" y2="101" marker-start="url(#sa-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sa-r-mk)"/>
            <text class="note note-live" x="110" y="58" text-anchor="end">ask</text>
            <text class="note note-live" x="270" y="58">ask</text>
            <text class="note note-live" x="190" y="94" text-anchor="middle">ask</text>
            <rect class="n shadow" x="130" y="10" width="120" height="32"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="190" y="30" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>
            <rect class="n-fail shadow" x="15" y="84" width="130" height="32"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="80" y="104" text-anchor="middle">Abject &middot; agent</text>
            <rect class="n shadow" x="235" y="84" width="130" height="32"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="300" y="104" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>
            <text class="note note-bone note-i" x="190" y="146" text-anchor="middle">no top: any abject can ask any other</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">In Abject an AI agent is just another abject. It doesn't sit on top of its tools. Any abject can ask any other one how it works and get an answer in plain English, so the tools talk back.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <!-- B: a paper field, the diagrams inked -->
  <article class="cmp cmp-field field-paper cut-top cut-bottom" id="vs-tool-protocols">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="cmp-head">
          <span class="cmp-letter" aria-hidden="true">B</span>
          <h3 class="cmp-title">Tool Protocols</h3>
          <span class="cmp-systems">MCP &middot; Claude Skills &middot; Function Calling</span>
        </header>
      <div class="field-pair">
        <div>
          <p class="fp-label ghosted">Them</p>
          <p class="fp-sub">a menu of functions</p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 408px" viewBox="0 0 340 170" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="A menu of functions: the LLM reads a fixed menu of functions that cannot speak">
            <defs>
              <marker id="sb-l-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <rect class="n-old shadow" x="120" y="10" width="100" height="36"/>
            <text class="lbl t-old-hi" x="170" y="33" text-anchor="middle">LLM</text>
            <line class="ln-old" x1="170" y1="46" x2="170" y2="66" marker-end="url(#sb-l-mk)"/>
            <rect class="n-old" x="85" y="70" width="170" height="52"/>
            <text class="note t-old" x="170" y="92" text-anchor="middle">{'{ "tools": ['}</text>
            <text class="note t-old" x="170" y="109" text-anchor="middle">{'  fn(), fn(), fn() ]}'}</text>
            <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="120" y1="122" x2="72" y2="142"/>
            <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="170" y1="122" x2="170" y2="142"/>
            <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="220" y1="122" x2="268" y2="142"/>
            <text class="note t-old" x="70" y="158" text-anchor="middle">fn()</text>
            <text class="note t-old" x="170" y="158" text-anchor="middle">fn()</text>
            <text class="note t-old" x="270" y="158" text-anchor="middle">fn()</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">MCP exposes tools as JSON-RPC functions with schemas. Claude Skills put instructions into the prompt. Both hand the LLM a menu to order from. The tools can't ask each other anything, so nothing negotiates, nothing heals, and nothing composes on its own.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fp-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div>
          <p class="fp-label hand">Abject</p>
          <p class="fp-sub">objects that negotiate</p>
          <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 470px" viewBox="-6 0 392 172" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Objects that negotiate: Abject A and Abject B have incompatible interfaces; the Negotiator reads both and generates a proxy abject that bridges them">
            <defs>
              <marker id="sb-r-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
              <marker id="sb-r-mk-bone" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path class="mk-bone" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <!-- Two abjects with incompatible interfaces -->
            <rect class="n shadow" x="10" y="10" width="100" height="44"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="60" y="29" text-anchor="middle">Abject A</text>
            <text class="note" x="60" y="46" text-anchor="middle">interface X</text>
            <rect class="n shadow" x="270" y="10" width="100" height="44"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="320" y="29" text-anchor="middle">Abject B</text>
            <text class="note" x="320" y="46" text-anchor="middle">interface Y</text>
            <!-- the direct link fails -->
            <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="112" y1="27" x2="172" y2="27"/>
            <line class="ln-old-dash" x1="208" y1="27" x2="268" y2="27"/>
            <text class="t-old" x="190" y="33" text-anchor="middle" style="font-size:18px">&ne;</text>
            <!-- the Living Proxy bridges them -->
            <line class="ln-live" x1="86" y1="56" x2="146" y2="75" marker-start="url(#sb-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sb-r-mk)"/>
            <line class="ln-live" x1="294" y1="56" x2="234" y2="75" marker-start="url(#sb-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sb-r-mk)"/>
            <rect class="n-key shadow" x="135" y="74" width="110" height="30"/>
            <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-key" x="190" y="94" text-anchor="middle">Proxy</text>
            <!-- the Negotiator reads both sides, then generates the proxy -->
            <rect class="n shadow" x="130" y="136" width="120" height="30"/>
            <text class="id" x="190" y="156" text-anchor="middle">Negotiator</text>
            <path class="ln-bone-dash" d="M 130 146 C 35 140 24 86 54 58" marker-end="url(#sb-r-mk-bone)"/>
            <path class="ln-bone-dash" d="M 250 146 C 345 140 356 86 326 58" marker-end="url(#sb-r-mk-bone)"/>
            <text class="note note-bone note-i" x="-4" y="136">reads both</text>
            <line class="ln-live" x1="190" y1="134" x2="190" y2="108" marker-end="url(#sb-r-mk)"/>
            <text class="note note-live note-i" x="198" y="126">generates</text>
          </svg>
          <p class="cmp-text">Every abject explains itself in plain English. When two abjects expect different messages, the Negotiator asks both of them how they work and writes a proxy between them. The proxy is a real abject too.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="container">
    <!-- C: one large drawing on the void, the two texts beneath -->
    <article class="cmp" id="vs-orchestration">
      <header class="cmp-head">
          <span class="cmp-letter" aria-hidden="true">C</span>
          <h3 class="cmp-title">Orchestration</h3>
          <span class="cmp-systems">AutoGen &middot; Subagents &middot; ReAct</span>
        </header>
      <div class="bigdg">
        <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 470px" viewBox="0 0 310 180" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="A hierarchy: an LLM Planner on top delegates to subagents, which call tools, with no lateral links">
          <defs>
            <marker id="sc-l-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-old" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <rect class="n-old shadow" x="95" y="10" width="120" height="34"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old-hi" x="155" y="32" text-anchor="middle">LLM Planner</text>
          <line class="ln-old" x1="128" y1="44" x2="82" y2="70" marker-end="url(#sc-l-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-old" x1="182" y1="44" x2="228" y2="70" marker-end="url(#sc-l-mk)"/>
          <rect class="n-old" x="25" y="73" width="110" height="28"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="80" y="92" text-anchor="middle">Subagent 1</text>
          <rect class="n-old" x="175" y="73" width="110" height="28"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-old" x="230" y="92" text-anchor="middle">Subagent 2</text>
          <line class="ln-old" x1="80" y1="101" x2="80" y2="121" marker-end="url(#sc-l-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-old" x1="230" y1="101" x2="230" y2="121" marker-end="url(#sc-l-mk)"/>
          <rect class="n-old" x="45" y="125" width="70" height="24"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="80" y="141" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text>
          <rect class="n-old" x="195" y="125" width="70" height="24"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-xs t-old" x="230" y="141" text-anchor="middle">Tool</text>
          <text class="note note-i" x="155" y="172" text-anchor="middle">no lateral links, LLM always on top</text>
        </svg>
        <div class="bigdg-div" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <svg class="dg" style="max-width: 570px" viewBox="0 0 380 176" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="No hierarchy: abjects talk to each other laterally, spawn new abjects that spawn more, and call the LLM as a service on demand">
          <defs>
            <marker id="sc-r-mk" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-live" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
            <marker id="sc-r-mk-bone" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
              <path class="mk-bone" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <!-- Abjects at the same level, linked laterally -->
          <rect class="n shadow" x="10" y="34" width="90" height="34"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="55" y="56" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>
          <rect class="n shadow" x="145" y="34" width="90" height="34"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="190" y="56" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>
          <rect class="n shadow" x="280" y="34" width="90" height="34"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm" x="325" y="56" text-anchor="middle">Abject</text>
          <line class="ln-live" x1="103" y1="51" x2="142" y2="51" marker-start="url(#sc-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sc-r-mk)"/>
          <line class="ln-live" x1="238" y1="51" x2="277" y2="51" marker-start="url(#sc-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sc-r-mk)"/>
          <path class="ln-live-dash" d="M 55 31 Q 190 2 325 31" marker-start="url(#sc-r-mk)" marker-end="url(#sc-r-mk)"/>
          <!-- an abject spawns an abject, which spawns another -->
          <line class="ln-bone" x1="55" y1="68" x2="55" y2="98" marker-end="url(#sc-r-mk-bone)"/>
          <rect class="n-dash" x="10" y="102" width="90" height="28"/>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="55" y="120" text-anchor="middle">spawned</text>
          <line class="ln-bone" x1="55" y1="130" x2="55" y2="146" marker-end="url(#sc-r-mk-bone)"/>
          <rect class="n-dash" x="22" y="149" width="66" height="22"/>
          <text class="note note-bone" x="55" y="164" text-anchor="middle">spawned</text>
          <!-- the LLM as a side service -->
          <line class="ln-bone-dash" x1="190" y1="68" x2="190" y2="98"/>
          <rect class="n-key shadow" x="150" y="100" width="80" height="28"/>
          <text class="lbl lbl-sm t-key" x="190" y="119" text-anchor="middle">LLM</text>
          <text class="note note-bone note-i" x="190" y="150" text-anchor="middle">on demand</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="bigdg-texts">
        <div>
          <p class="side-label">Them &middot; a hierarchy</p>
          <p class="cmp-text">AutoGen orchestrates conversations between LLMs. Coding agents spawn subagents in fresh contexts, one level deep by design. The LLM sits at the top, planning and handing out work, and the programs underneath are just material it moves around.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="side-label hand">Abject &middot; no hierarchy, the LLM is a service</p>
          <p class="cmp-text">The LLM is just another abject, a service the others call when they need it. Abjects can create abjects, which can create more abjects, and there is no limit on how deep that goes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- D: the split reversed, Abject first -->
    <article class="cmp" id="vs-visual-interface">
      <header class="cmp-head">
          <span class="cmp-letter" aria-hidden="true">D</span>
          <h3 class="cmp-title">Visual Interface</h3>
          <span class="cmp-systems">ChatGPT &middot; Claude &middot; Terminal Agents</span>
        </header>
      <div class="split">
        <div class="ghost">
          <p class="side-label">Them <span class="sub">text in, text out</span></p>
